{"t": 187.41, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 1, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "sshi_fbr", "rationale": "The reference FBR failed because the piezo's open-circuit voltage (approx 0.76 V) is below the required 1.8 V output. I am implementing a Synchronized Switch Harvesting on Inductor (SSHI) circuit. This uses an inductor and a switch to flip the voltage across the piezo capacitance at every peak, effectively 'pumping' the voltage to a higher level that can then be rectified and stored. A full-bridge rectifier (FBR) is used for efficient energy extraction from both halves of the cycle, and a Zener diode clamps the output to 3.3 V to satisfy the vmax limit.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "sshi_fbr", "rationale": "The reference FBR failed because the piezo's open-circuit voltage (approx 0.76 V) is below the required 1.8 V output. I am implementing a Synchronized Switch Harvesting on Inductor (SSHI) circuit. This uses an inductor and a switch to flip the voltage across the piezo capacitance at every peak, effectively 'pumping' the voltage to a higher level that can then be rectified and stored. A full-bridge rectifier (FBR) is used for efficient energy extraction from both halves of the cycle, and a Zener diode clamps the output to 3.3 V to satisfy the vmax limit.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.0047}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 3.4e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzp"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D4", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzn"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "Cout", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 1e-06}, {"id": "Dz", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}]}}
