{"t": 496.57, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 2, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "sshi_doubler", "rationale": "The previous 'sshi_fbr' failed due to slow startup and settling (high dv), which indicates that the power delivered to the storage capacitor drops significantly as Vout rises. This is likely due to the diode drops of the full-bridge rectifier competing with the piezo's boosted voltage. By replacing the full-bridge with a voltage-doubler (Greinacher cell) architecture, we effectively double the voltage seen by the output diodes, allowing for much higher power delivery at Vout = 1.8-3.6V. This allows the use of a smaller Cout, which will fix the startup time (tup) and the settling time (dv) while maintaining low ripple.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "sshi_doubler", "rationale": "The previous 'sshi_fbr' failed due to slow startup and settling (high dv), which indicates that the power delivered to the storage capacitor drops significantly as Vout rises. This is likely due to the diode drops of the full-bridge rectifier competing with the piezo's boosted voltage. By replacing the full-bridge with a voltage-doubler (Greinacher cell) architecture, we effectively double the voltage seen by the output diodes, allowing for much higher power delivery at Vout = 1.8-3.6V. This allows the use of a smaller Cout, which will fix the startup time (tup) and the settling time (dv) while maintaining low ripple.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "value": 0.0047}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 3.4e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "n2"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes": ["n2", "0"], "value": 1e-07}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["n2", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "n3"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "C2", "type": "C", "nodes": ["n3",