{"t": 1295.5, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 5, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "sshi_dual_doubler", "rationale": "The previous best design (sshi_fbr) failed only on the ripple requirement for the strong excitation case (S3). This suggests the charge pulses from the SSHI are creating spikes that the storage capacitor cannot fully buffer, and the Zener is clipping the peaks. I am replacing the full-bridge rectifier with a dual-doubler (two Greinacher circuits). This topology uses intermediate capacitors to buffer the charge from both the positive and negative half-cycles before it reaches the output. This distributed charge delivery should naturally reduce the high-frequency ripple and allow the optimizer to find a more stable output voltage across all conditions, especially S3, while still maintaining the fast startup and efficiency of the SSHI.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "sshi_dual_doubler", "rationale": "The previous best design (sshi_fbr) failed only on the ripple requirement for the strong excitation case (S3). This suggests the charge pulses from the SSHI are creating spikes that the storage capacitor cannot fully buffer, and the Zener is clipping the peaks. I am replacing the full-bridge rectifier with a dual-doubler (two Greinacher circuits). This topology uses intermediate capacitors to buffer the charge from both the positive and negative half-cycles before it reaches the output. This distributed charge delivery should naturally reduce the high-frequency ripple and allow the optimizer to find a more stable output voltage across all conditions, especially S3, while still maintaining the fast startup and efficiency of the SSHI.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.0064}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 3.7e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "mid1"], "model": "DSCH